{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 4a (08ab) — spec + surface-parity census + API design.\n\nhcl2 8.1.3 API CONFIRMED by probe: parses_to_tree(text)->lark Tree; internal _get_parser().options.propagate_positions=True; block nodes carry .meta (line,col,end_line,end_col); block children = identifier(type)+string(labels)+body; loads()->dict with __is_block__ markers. Positions from tree, addressing from loads dict.\n\nSURFACE-PARITY CENSUS for 08ab (slice scope = plan-review only): CLI=n/a (no new CLI verb); MCP/API tool=the grounding tools are exposed to LLM agents via workflow RunnerAgentStep extra_tools, tested through plan-review Pass-1/Pass-2 routing (IN SCOPE); library facade=rebar.grounding.terraform_tools + terraform_index public import (IN SCOPE, lean-import tested); automated callers=plan-review workflow finder/verifier (IN SCOPE); dual-direction=n/a for v1. Code-review surface is OUT OF SCOPE here (slice afe3). probe_source/corroborate_diagnostic OUT OF SCOPE (slices 1c52/c6ce).\n\nOBSERVABLE TOOL API (fixed by held-out oracle, implementer must match):\n- rebar.grounding.terraform_index: LIMITS={modules:64,files:5000,bytes:33554432,timeout_ms:60000}; builds bounded module-closure snapshot from (root, selected paths); rejects out-of-repo/escaping symlinks; over-limit -> abstain reason 'other'/{module_limit|file_limit|byte_limit}.\n- rebar.grounding.terraform_tools: per-call session with lookup_declaration(address, module_path='') and resolve_reference(reference, from_file); each returns evidence (grounding.schema shape: refuted|abstain, job=refute, tier T1) + canonical receipt (terraform_grounding_receipt.schema). finalize() -> synthetic concrete reads + membership globs (**/*.tf, **/*.tf.json).\n- schema constant schemas.TERRAFORM_GROUNDING_RECEIPT.\n\nHELD-OUT SPLIT: happy-path (basic lookup refuted+receipt, basic resolve child-output, lean import) stays for implementer; edge/E2E (full abstention table, redaction, no-exec census, path escape, over-limit, membership-glob freshness, T10 Pass1/Pass2 routing) held out for orchestrator validation.\n\nNEXT: author RED tests, run them RED, hold out edge/E2E, dispatch implementation subagent."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788481981103105459,"uuid":"946023cf-2d67-494c-97c4-ea102a3a369a"}